        <mxCell id="c84" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Every &lt;font color=&#39;#B85450&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;red&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; pin connects to the Arduino &lt;b&gt;5V&lt;/b&gt; pin; every &lt;b&gt;grey&lt;/b&gt; pin connects to &lt;b&gt;GND&lt;/b&gt; (one common ground).&lt;br&gt;• I2C runs at &lt;b&gt;100 kHz&lt;/b&gt; (PCF8574 limit). LCD 0x27/0x3F, MPU6050 0x68. Both modules have on-board pull-ups.&lt;br&gt;• SPI to the matrices: D11 MOSI, D13 SCK (also drives the on-board &#39;L&#39; LED), D10 CS.&lt;br&gt;• Q1 PN2222A / 2N2222A TO-92, flat face towards you, legs down: &lt;b&gt;E – B – C&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;• LCD contrast: adjust the blue trimmer on the backpack if the screen is blank or shows solid blocks.&lt;br&gt;• Optional: 100 µF electrolytic across 5V/GND near the matrices to stop USB brown-outs." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="440" x="40" y="600" as="geometry" />
